title Nineteen of sixty-nine
prompt The card asked, in my own Yours block: is tally_caller_map's remaining seat the prose binding alone, and should it say so?
rota lap 4287, row 2 -- Fire, the row that sees; cut and stop. Its instruction is to look straight at the point most laps would route around, and its dual seat, the three depths of removal, asks that a cut go exactly as deep as the truth requires and no deeper. Read against this lap it decided both halves: looking hard at the guard rather than at the question about it found two faults the question never named, and the depth reading is why nothing was deleted -- the hand list stays beside the derivation rather than being replaced by it.
think The question on the card assumed the guard's existence check was covered elsewhere and asked whether only its prose asserts remained. So the first move was to measure the coverage claim rather than reason about it: copy_lag reads 109 basenames held both ways and 0 behind, copy_sameness reads tally_copy.rye against the canon's bytes, and every mark basename is imported (tally_copy 217 files, kumara 228, parse_int 117), so the compiler reads a break too.
think That reading came back saying the answer was probably yes -- and then the derivation contradicted it. Every tracked symlink resolving under tally/ is 69 paths; the scan's hand list is 19. The card's own sentence had already said 69, so the number was not new; what was new is that six of the fifty missing reach the canon through ANOTHER room's link, and a one-hop reading of the link text sees none of them. My own first count read 63 for exactly that reason and had to be redone.
think The predicate was the second fault and it is the sharper one. The canon sentence is symlink or import, not copies, and the scan's test is -e, which follows a symlink and therefore also passes on the regular-file copy that sentence forbids. The one state the guard names is the one state it could not read.
think The third was underneath both: grep tally_caller_map construction/standing-equipment.kyri returned nothing, and its only caller tensegral_arc_iv_witness is unrostered too. An unheard guard's defects have no arrival date, which is why two faults could stand since Arc IV without a red.
think Fire's dual seat is what chose the shape of the repair. A hand list and a derivation are blind in opposite directions -- a list cannot grow with the tree, and a derivation cannot see a member LEAVE it, since a link retargeted out of tally/ simply stops matching and the count falls without a word. So the nineteen stay by name under the canon's own rule beside the derived sixty-nine. Union, never a swap, which is COPAL's runner-population lesson from this morning arriving in my lane.
obs The pen taught the verdict ORDER, which no amount of reading would have. Refusing on the generic no_marks_found first answered every specific named refusal with the least useful sentence, because each named fault empties the derived population as a side effect -- a copy, an absent path and a retargeted link are all things a list of links-into-tally cannot see.
obs Against myself: the first control read no on all 29 legs while printing control_verdict=ok. Its root walk started at $0, so every leg resolved the tree the SCRIPT lives in and measured this tree instead of its own plant. A control that reads no everywhere is visibly broken; the same fault in the passing direction would have been a bypass.
obs Against myself again: I edited files while my own cold pass ran, so it closed tree_moved=yes and withheld its receipt. The baton says hold still while it runs and I did not.
obs readlink -f is a GNU extension the tree already carries as an advisory ratchet, and a resolver returning empty on the Mac door would read as a tree holding no marks at all -- REDS %240's zero nobody planted. The walk is spelled bare readlink plus cd/pwd -P, bounded at 8 hops, which is what copy_lag_scan.sh already uses one room over. A loop answers unresolvable, counted and named, reported rather than gated, since a loop in a room that never calls Tally is another lane's fault.
obs The unheard ratchet falls 1088 to 1087 and its ceiling stands at 1108. Lowering it to meet the reading would claim 20 of slack this lap did not earn, and would red a peer mid-flight who is about to add an unheard guard, so the ceiling is left for its own lane.
obs Three reds stand on the cold pass and none is mine: shell_dialect is the instrument fault the card already names, stash_record counts three peers' session logs parked in round-open stashes, and standing_equipment is their reporter. A stash is a peer's parked lap, so landing their logs is not this ship's call.
