obs The pin refused the commit before the round did, twice, and the second time was the honest one. construction/REDS.md stood over its declared 40,960 with 13 of 15 rows OPEN, so the commit hook, reds_pin_capacity, declared_ceiling and the e123 pin guard all reddened on one root. My first answer folded %622; the rebase showed a peer had already folded that same row to a shelf of their own an hour earlier, so my fold and its shelf withdrew whole and the row folded is this lap's own.
obs Two rebases renumbered my row twice and withdrew one whole artifact. Peers published %627 and then %628 for different incidents while mine stood unshared, so it derives above each in turn and lands at %629 -- and each move cost ONE line, in the ledger itself, because every living citation already spells the stamp. That is derived-spine rules 3 and 4 paying for themselves twice inside forty minutes. The withdrawal was the fold: my first answer to the over-bound pin folded %622, and the rebase showed a peer had folded that same row an hour earlier to a shelf of their own, so my shelf and my recital line left whole and this lap's own row folded instead.
scope one guard in the tally lane -- reach, predicate, and clock -- plus the canon prose it binds
status GREEN -- tally_caller_map_witness and tensegral_arc_iv_witness both pass on metal, control 32 of 32, scan reads 69 marks with every gated count at zero; the three cold-pass reds are pre-existing and named above
